He does not, however, dismiss crypto after saying that gains are not cashflow. Instead he reframes it as a value problem. In his telling, the deeper question is not only whether crypto went up, but why a society treats something as valuable at all: $\begin{aligned}
V &\stackrel{?}{\propto} \text{scarcity},\\
V &\stackrel{?}{\propto} \text{scarcity}+E,\end{aligned}$ where $V$ is perceived value and $E$ is extraction or verification cost.

