But Miller does not stop at contribution. He adds values and destination. The business becomes fragile if the partners are not aligned on where they are going and what standards they share under stress. In that sense the partnership test has two layers: $\text{partner fit}
=
\text{real contribution}
+
\text{values alignment}.$ The plus sign here is verbal, not numerical. It preserves the lecture’s combined test: useful tools without aligned purpose are unstable, and aligned sentiment without useful contribution is weak.

